CONTRACT DEFINITION:
1. RESEARCH NOTE: See plan/005_95d30743cdd4/bugfix/001_3f1132e1694f/architecture/bug_verification.md §BUG-006 and architecture/spec_requirements.md §BUG-006. In src/transforms.ts, resolveLastTurn (line ~345) returns `{ remove: [] }` when `iFirstUser === iLastUser` (nuclear on the first user message — the protected boundary). In src/tools/rewind.ts, rewindExecute step 5 calls resolvePreview which internally calls resolveLastTurn. When resolveLastTurn returns {remove:[]}, resolvePreview returns {ledger: emptyLedger, k:0, hideEntryIds:[]}. The tool then proceeds to step 6 (render note) and step 7 (persist marker with empty hideEntryIds + leave note) — violating spec/08 E3 ('the tool refuses before persisting').
2. INPUT: The rewindExecute function in src/tools/rewind.ts, specifically the region between step 5 (resolvePreview, lines 538-548) and step 6 (renderNote, line 551). The `params` object has `granularity` and `to_previous_prompt`. The `k` value from resolvePreview is 0 for this case, but k===0 is ALSO a legitimate result for last_tool_call_group (nothing to hide). The DISTINGUISHING signal is: granularity==='last_turn' AND to_previous_prompt===true AND k===0 AND hideEntryIds.length===0 — this combination only occurs when resolveLastTurn returned the protected refusal.
3. LOGIC: Add a guarded check AFTER resolvePreview returns and BEFORE step 6 (renderNote) / step 7 (persist):
    // (5b) Protected-refusal check (spec/08 E3): nuclear last_turn on the first user message.
    //      resolveLastTurn returns {remove:[]} for this protected case. The ONLY way
    //      granularity==='last_turn' + to_previous_prompt===true produces k===0 with
    //      empty hideEntryIds is this protected refusal — a normal last_turn always finds
    //      at least one message after the user prompt (the rewind's own call).
    if (
      granularity === 'last_turn' &&
      params.to_previous_prompt === true &&
      k === 0 &&
      hideEntryIds.length === 0
    ) {
      return refuse('would cross the protected first:user boundary (cannot nuclear-rewind the original task)', granularity);
    }
  Place this AFTER the resolvePreview try/catch block (step 5) and BEFORE step 6 (renderNote). The refuse() closure already handles the rewindRefusedTurnIndex flag (P4.M1.T2.S3). This ensures the marker is NOT persisted and NO note is left.
4. OUTPUT: The modified src/tools/rewind.ts file. A nuclear last_turn rewind on the first/only user message now returns `Mulligan: refused — would cross the protected first:user boundary (cannot nuclear-rewind the original task).` WITHOUT persisting any marker or note. The depth counter (countRewindMarkers) is NOT incremented. A normal nuclear last_turn (with a prior user message) is unaffected.
5. DOCS: [Mode A] Add a comment at the new check (step 5b) explaining the E3 contract: 'spec/08 E3: the tool refuses before persisting when the rewind would cross a protected message.' Also update the step numbering comment for subsequent steps if needed. This rides WITH the work.

